 Run its tests with `npm test`.
+
+`importTasks(list, text)` adds tasks from lines formatted as `title;priority;tags`, for example
+`Renew the insurance;high;admin money`. Each nonblank line must have exactly three semicolon-separated
+fields. Fields are trimmed; an empty priority uses `normal`, and tags are separated by whitespace.
+Empty tags are allowed. Blank lines are skipped. The helper returns `{ imported, rejected }`, where
+`imported` counts added tasks and `rejected` contains `{ line, reason }` entries with one-based source
+line numbers and explanatory messages. Invalid rows and duplicate titles are rejected without
+stopping the remaining rows.
